From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] d3dx9: D3DXValidMesh, skin info influences, tangent frame argument checks

Results the Wine tests record from Windows (todo) and the stubs next to them.

 - D3DXValidMesh finds a face that uses a vertex twice, an index out of range, and a bow-tie vertex
   (the faces around a vertex are not one fan by the adjacency): D3DXERR_INVALIDMESH with a message
   in errors_and_warnings; a valid mesh is D3D_OK.
 - ID3DXSkinInfo: SetBoneVertexInfluence, GetBoneVertexInfluence, FindBoneVertexInfluenceIndex,
   GetMaxVertexInfluences (the most bones that influence a vertex, 0 without bones), GetMaxFaceInfluences
   (the most bones that influence the three vertices of a face) and Set/GetMinBoneInfluence are
   implemented instead of returning E_NOTIMPL.
 - D3DXComputeTangentFrameEx returns D3DERR_INVALIDCALL when nothing is to be computed, and when the mesh is
   not changed in place and no output mesh is asked for.
 - D3DXLoadSkinMeshFromXof of a file without vertices returns D3DXERR_LOADEDMESHASNODATA (the mesh
   loaders inside the library still take it as no mesh).
 - Removed the todo marks of these checks in mesh.c.
